    "An apparent cause evaluation is less thorough than a root cause but still provides for a thoughtful evaluation of the occurrence. A apparent cause does not usually identify actions to prevent recurrence, but may if the cause is very obvious. The actions are focused on remediation of the problem and on proximate causes. An extent of condition can be performed for a root cause evaluation.": 1,
